WEBVTT

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:16.430
She's the spitting image of His Majesty.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:19.180
She's a lovely little princess.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.310
I see.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.810
A girl? It will be a prince next time.

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:29.570
Once an heir is born, the Duke
of Clarence will lose his place.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.480
Just like the Earl of Warwick.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.740
Why?!

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:36.740
Why can't I marry Isabelle?!

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.080
Some are uneasy about your
growing too close to Warwick.

00:00:41.080 --> 00:00:42.700
Who's been saying that?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.170
Did that woman put you up to this?

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.680
York of the white rose.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.260
Lancaster of the red rose.

00:00:59.260 --> 00:01:05.730
These royal houses with roses for
their crests battled for the throne.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.570
People call their strife
the "Wars of the Roses."

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.750
Lift your head, Margaret.

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.880
The haughty and ambitious Edward

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:57.300
now proclaims himself the
rightful King of England.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:58.970
But the true king is...

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:02.260
Yes, the true king, my father is...

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:06.010
If only I had been quicker to find him!

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:12.810
What's going on?
What is Father doing with Richard?!

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.150
Wasn't the throne enough?!
Does he plan to take everything from me?!

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:27.990
But King Henry yet lives.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:30.330
Time is of the essence.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.420
The enemy's strength grows even as we--

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.880
Oh, I see you've arrived.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:41.630
What are <i>you</i>...

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.510
...doing here?!

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.260
You shameless familiar of York!

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:51.100
Damn you!

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.020
Your Majesty, my virtuous queen.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.230
Sheathe your sword, Prince.

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.570
He is none other than your savior.

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:07.700
Warwick is going to save us?!

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.160
Your Majesty, I beg you
to forget our past enmity.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:22.170
I too have been dishonored
by the rebel Edward.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:25.470
Henceforth, I wish to become
your loyal servant

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:31.680
and to restore King Henry
to his proper station.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:35.980
You speak as though you've become God.

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.110
Your Majesty.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.820
I'm delighted, Warwick.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:49.950
Your words have turned
all my hatred into love.

00:04:49.950 --> 00:04:53.080
If you and I...

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.210
...and the King of France join forces,

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.880
we should be able to depose
the false king in short order.

00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:01.880
Mother.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:08.550
But only if you can provide proof
that you are not deceiving me.

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:09.550
Proof?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:13.850
What I desire is...

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.560
...your love.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:24.570
In token of which, give your eldest
daughter Anne to my prince in marriage.

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.210
Is anything the matter,

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.880
Crown Prince Edward?

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.880
How are York's sons?

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:46.220
Say... Richard, for example?

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:50.430
Richard currently resides at my castle.

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:51.930
My daughter is with him, and--

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:54.270
I see! He's at your castle.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.020
I don't want to marry Warwick's daughter,

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:02.020
but Mother would never let me refuse.

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:06.280
Still, before I'm married,
I want to see her!

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.610
To see Richard!

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:13.280
Warwick, please, take me to England!

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:23.380
Richard.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:26.090
Richard!

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:27.420
I've found you!

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:30.180
Stay back!

00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:31.300
Richard?

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:34.350
I'm sure you'd leave me too,

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:36.430
if you knew the real me.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:40.520
That's not true.
I'll stay with you always.

00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.270
Duke Richard!

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.400
--Anne.
--Duke Richard,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:47.860
it's been so hard for me.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.950
Pretending to like you, I mean.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:54.240
After all, the truth is...

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.830
I actually despise you!

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:02.920
Richard!

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.170
Stay away.

00:07:04.170 --> 00:07:06.960
Stop it. I can't take anymore.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:12.550
Richard!

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.030
There's no one else here.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:33.740
No one to hurt you and no one to love you.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.660
This is a royal palace just for you.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.210
Father, what's come over you?

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.550
Where is Anne?

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.930
My lady sister is...

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.590
Who is this?

00:07:53.590 --> 00:07:55.720
Wait in the drawing room.

00:07:55.720 --> 00:07:58.100
I will bring Anne to you shortly.

00:07:58.100 --> 00:08:00.930
All right. You needn't rush.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:09.150
I've done my best to mend relations
between Anne and Gloucester, but--

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.740
That no longer matters.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:15.280
I've decided to take you both to France.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:16.830
What's brought this on?

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:21.160
George will accompany us.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:32.510
Then it's finally time to begin?

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:37.260
Where on earth is she?

00:08:37.260 --> 00:08:39.640
What are you doing there?

00:08:39.640 --> 00:08:41.180
Richard!

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:43.100
You're not of this castle.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:47.560
I-I only just arrived with Warwick!

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:50.980
I took a stroll and got
separated from him.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:54.900
Do you remember, Richard?

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:59.370
I kissed those lips of yours.

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:01.700
Duke Richard!

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:02.830
Anne.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.500
This is her?

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:08.920
I found lots of raspberries growing
in the woods the other day.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:12.920
Would you come with me to pick some?

00:09:12.920 --> 00:09:14.920
We could go on horseback again and--

00:09:14.920 --> 00:09:16.470
Anne.

00:09:16.470 --> 00:09:19.050
You needn't force yourself anymore.

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:20.930
I release you.

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:27.270
I'd thank you not to wander off alone.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:35.900
Warwick, I will return to the king.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:37.320
I'm sorry to hear it.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.410
"Sorry"? That's an odd response.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.830
I thank you. This is all the
result of your tutelage.

00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:54.010
I'll never let my emotions sway me
and lose sight of my position again.

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.300
This was the last time.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.600
Why don't you stop Richard?!

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:08.100
Your mother took the stake
I'd planned to tie him to.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:12.110
What stake? You mean Anne?

00:10:12.110 --> 00:10:13.860
I see.

00:10:13.860 --> 00:10:18.610
Still, it looked to me like your daughter
has feelings for Richard.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:22.120
A child's fancy, soon forgotten.

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.950
I can't be so sure.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.410
I know you. Who knows when
you'll change your mind

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:32.420
and start plotting to marry Anne
to Richard after all.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:36.460
This is the last they'll ever see
of each other. The very last.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:43.050
I can't trust you until I've seen you
bring down the king with my own eyes.

00:10:43.050 --> 00:10:45.310
What do you intend to do, then?

00:10:45.310 --> 00:10:48.060
I'll stay until that happens.

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.610
If we reclaim the throne, I should be
free to decide Richard's fate.

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:58.990
Anyone who gets in my way
can rot in the Tower until they die.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:02.700
Very well. I won't object.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:10.290
You'll get your chance to see the moment
the king falls to his knees.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:13.590
To arms!

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.550
Have you heard the rebel
army's proclamations?

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:23.260
They claim you've betrayed
the old nobility

00:11:23.260 --> 00:11:27.680
and shown undue favor to
my family, the Woodvilles.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:32.060
Nonsense, although I have
heard similar rumors before.

00:11:32.060 --> 00:11:35.110
Too much worry is bad for your health.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:38.190
You're showing signs of another
pregnancy, remember?

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:39.860
True.

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:45.530
That's right, and that's why I can't
have you dying on me just yet.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.870
Not until I give birth to an heir.

00:11:55.130 --> 00:11:58.510
This clamor. The weight of steel.

00:11:58.510 --> 00:12:02.050
Tension and excitement
that make me tremble.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:05.100
I've come home to the battlefield.

00:12:05.760 --> 00:12:09.890
What a shame that the Duke
of Clarence is in France.

00:12:09.890 --> 00:12:12.810
He'll miss Gloucester's first campaign.

00:12:12.810 --> 00:12:17.610
It's not just George.
Warwick isn't here either.

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:19.610
Your Majesty, a message.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:21.700
Is that a coincidence?

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:26.370
I don't believe it!

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.410
I never gave him my permission.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:34.120
George has married Isabelle Neville.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:44.180
Your Majesty, I believe a temporary
retreat would be advisable.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:45.590
Why?

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:50.020
It's possible that George
is in league with Warwick.

00:12:50.020 --> 00:12:52.810
They may plan to rebel
against Your Majesty.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:56.060
Why? What would drive them to rebellion?

00:12:56.060 --> 00:13:01.610
Your Majesty, there are rumors that the
Earl of Warwick instigated this uprising.

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:04.950
Let's return to London
and augment our forces.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:07.200
Hastings is correct, my lord brother!

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:11.580
Marrying without your permission
is a clear act of rebellion!

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:14.830
You must punish him severely
to ensure that he can never defy us--

00:13:14.830 --> 00:13:15.830
Anthony!

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.880
George is my brother by blood.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:24.840
And I've faced deadly danger with Warwick;
he's more than a brother to me.

00:13:26.470 --> 00:13:29.850
If those two ever betrayed me, then...

00:13:31.100 --> 00:13:33.350
But that could never happen.

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:50.450
That dream again.

00:13:53.790 --> 00:13:56.080
There's no one else here.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:59.420
This is a royal palace just for you.

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.800
I feel at ease in there.

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:05.800
But there's no palace for me in reality.

00:14:05.800 --> 00:14:07.550
That'd never happen.

00:14:07.550 --> 00:14:11.890
Just suppose. If the Earl of Warwick
defeats King Edward,

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.720
the Duke of Clarence
could be the new king.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:18.190
Attack!

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:22.650
Edward!

00:14:22.650 --> 00:14:23.820
Where's the king?!

00:14:23.820 --> 00:14:25.740
Aim for the king's tent!

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.490
Defend His Majesty!

00:14:37.960 --> 00:14:39.670
Hurry up and run!

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:41.750
Hey, women came out of that tent!

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.290
Have you found the duke?!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:44.840
I need a weapon.

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.720
I don't see Richard anywhere!

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:50.140
Search everywhere!

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.680
Move, woman. You're in my way.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:08.240
Are you really a woman?

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:11.360
I hear the king's little brother
is awfully small.

00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:14.240
Well, we'll find out once
the bosses see you.

00:15:14.240 --> 00:15:17.750
Lord Warwick and the
Duke of Clarence, I mean.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:21.830
I knew it! So, he really
is after the throne!

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.380
Got that? Now, come with me.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:24.500
Wait.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.130
H-Hey.

00:15:28.970 --> 00:15:31.380
Here's your proof.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:42.150
I never thought this body of
mine would prove useful.

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.520
I need to rejoin the main force quickly.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:51.490
What a wanton woman.
You picked a fine time to tempt a man.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:53.950
Tell me, was the king's thing good?

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:55.410
St-Stop!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.330
Your Grace!

00:16:05.540 --> 00:16:07.170
--Catesby.
--This way!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:12.680
I confirmed that His Royal Majesty
and Lord Hastings went this way.

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:16.810
Why didn't you go with Hastings?
He's your lord.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:19.850
I didn't see you with them.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:24.440
What could be more natural than a knight
of the realm defending the royal family?

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:28.940
I know I've told you not to let
loyalty to my father bind you.

00:16:31.650 --> 00:16:33.530
My humble apologies.

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:35.740
Don't mind me. I can run.

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:38.580
We need to rejoin Edward
as soon as possible.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:41.710
I beg your pardon.

00:16:41.710 --> 00:16:43.290
Hey! There he is!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.170
Over here!

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:45.540
Come quick!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:47.130
We caught the king!

00:16:52.840 --> 00:16:57.390
Warwick? How could you repay
my trust with treachery?

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:03.270
That's a poor jest, Edward.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:07.610
"Edward"? You called me your king.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:12.650
Edward, it was you who betrayed my trust.

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:16.740
You cast me down and disgraced me.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:21.290
Warwick, mend your speech
and call me king this instant.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.540
Do that, and I'll forgive you all your--

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:26.960
It appears that you have yet
to grasp your position.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:32.630
You are no longer my king, nor are you
worthy to govern the kingdom.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:39.140
I will reclaim the land and return
it to its rightful sovereign.

00:17:39.140 --> 00:17:42.100
What "rightful sovereign"?

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:47.190
He is here now.

00:17:47.190 --> 00:17:52.440
King George is my true sovereign,
and I, his vassal.

00:17:56.950 --> 00:17:58.990
I see no signs of pursuit.

00:17:58.990 --> 00:18:02.080
Whatever hogwash Warwick
used to justify this,

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:04.950
George could never take the throne.

00:18:04.950 --> 00:18:07.870
Assuming that King Edward
lives, of course.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:14.920
Catesby, you said that it's natural
for a knight to defend royalty.

00:18:14.920 --> 00:18:20.220
Tell me; what would you do
if I betrayed the king?

00:18:20.220 --> 00:18:23.850
What would you do if I sought the throne?

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:34.190
Your Grace.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:38.610
I will...

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.950
...defend the Royal Family of York.

00:18:43.950 --> 00:18:48.330
Your lord father saved my life.

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:52.670
It is my destiny to follow
the House of York.

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.720
Everyone must want a follower like you.

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.470
Think, Richard.

00:19:02.890 --> 00:19:05.270
What's the best choice?

00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:07.850
Who is most worthy of the throne?

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:16.150
Unless I fight, I'll lose everything

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:18.190
to those who have no right.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:25.830
Now that the king has been defeated,
who does England belong to?

00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:30.000
Who is sitting on the throne now?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.040
Elizabeth! The king was ambushed!

00:19:33.040 --> 00:19:34.670
The king is dead?

00:19:34.670 --> 00:19:37.420
N-No, but they took him prisoner.

00:19:37.420 --> 00:19:38.380
Your Majesty!

00:19:38.380 --> 00:19:41.220
Lord Warwick and the Duke of
Clarence are leading troops here!

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.800
What?!

00:19:42.800 --> 00:19:46.140
Warwick, that foolish man.

00:19:48.350 --> 00:19:51.850
If you're going to flee,
take my wife with you.

00:19:51.850 --> 00:19:54.480
She's one of your little sisters.

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:57.360
Come with us yourself, Buckingham.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:58.570
Make ready!

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:01.490
Why should I go with
the women and children?

00:20:01.490 --> 00:20:03.280
Hey, Anthony.

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.780
What about Richard?

00:20:04.780 --> 00:20:06.790
I haven't heard of his capture.

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:11.750
I'm more concerned about my father.
Warwick wants revenge on our whole family!

00:20:11.750 --> 00:20:13.580
He'll kill us all!

00:20:13.580 --> 00:20:16.130
I'll never let him do that.

00:20:17.340 --> 00:20:18.880
Never.

00:20:20.720 --> 00:20:24.050
Once you have the queen,
take her directly to the Tower.

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:26.510
Treat her with the utmost care.

00:20:26.510 --> 00:20:28.010
Yes, sir!

00:20:28.010 --> 00:20:31.310
After all, pregnant women die so easily.

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:38.190
I'll never let Warwick have his way.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:41.950
My vengeance isn't over yet.

00:20:46.030 --> 00:20:48.620
Why, Duke of Buckingham.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:51.370
Have you seen the queen, by any chance?

00:20:51.370 --> 00:20:53.330
What would you do if I had?

00:20:53.330 --> 00:21:00.010
You're an intelligent fellow. You ought to
know what the safest course is.

00:21:00.010 --> 00:21:06.300
Once Edward and the queen's family
are gone, George will be the new king?

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:11.680
But in that case, the next in line
to the throne would be...

00:21:11.680 --> 00:21:15.650
Of course, my lord. If I see her,
I'll inform you at once.

00:21:17.730 --> 00:21:18.860
We're leaving.

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.150
This chance is too good to pass up.

00:21:24.150 --> 00:21:26.820
If the throne rests on
unsteady foundations...

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.080
Hey. Search for Richard.

00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:32.790
Find him before Warwick.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:34.290
Yes, sir.

00:21:34.290 --> 00:21:37.420
I've decided to make you my king.

00:21:39.040 --> 00:21:42.170
A man who has no awareness as king.

00:21:42.170 --> 00:21:45.130
A man who is unqualified to be king.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:48.850
Neither of them is fit for the throne.

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.010
Even so,

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:54.810
Warwick, I will never, <i>never</i>
give the kingdom to you.

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:59.690
We're going to rescue King Edward.
